{"label": "engine_4users", "streams": [{"prompt": "Write a Python function that merges overlapping intervals in a list of [start, end] pairs, then a few pytest test cases for it. Keep the explanation short.", "chunks": [[0.0557, "```"], [0.0943, "python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals:"], [0.1715, " list[list[int]]) -> list"], [0.2579, "[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"Merge"], [0.3545, " overlapping intervals in a list of [start"], [0.4047, ", end] pairs.\"\"\"\n    if"], [0.4554, " not intervals:\n        return []\n"], [0.5066, "    \n    # Sort by start time\n"], [0.5576, "    intervals.sort(key=lambda x: x"], [0.609, "[0])\n    \n    merged ="], [0.6607, " [intervals[0]]\n   "], [0.7125, " for current in"], [0.7644, " intervals[1:]:\n        last"], [0.8169, " = merged[-1]\n        if"], [0.869, " current[0] <= last[1"], [0.922, "]:\n            # Overlapping"], [0.975, ": extend the end"], [1.0281, " if needed\n            last"], [1.0807, "[1] = max(last[1"], [1.1329, "], current[1])\n        else"], [1.1845, ":\n            merged.append(current)\n"], [1.2357, "    \n    return merged\n"], [1.2872, "```\n\n```python\nimport pytest"], [1.3383, "\nfrom merge_intervals import"], [1.3894, " merge_intervals\n\ndef test_empty"], [1.441, "_list():\n    assert merge_intervals([]"], [1.4919, ") == []\n\ndef test_single_interval"], [1.5431, "():\n    assert merge_intervals([[1"], [1.5943, ", 3]]) == [[1"], [1.6455, ", 3]]\n\ndef test_no"], [1.6963, "_overlap():\n    assert"], [1.748, " merge_intervals([[1, 2],"], [1.7995, " [4, 5]]) == [["], [1.8474, "1, 2], [4,"], [1.8954, " 5]]\n\ndef test_over"], [1.9438, "lapping_intervals():\n    assert"], [1.9925, " merge_intervals([[1, 3],"], [2.0413, " [2, 6], [8"], [2.0898, ", 10]]) == [[1"], [2.1384, ", 6], [8, "], [2.1861, "10]]\n\ndef test_contained"], [2.2338, "_interval():\n    assert"], [2.2806, " merge_intervals([[1, 1"], [2.3281, "0], [2, 5"], [2.3753, "]]) == [[1, 10"], [2.4229, "]]\n\ndef test_touching_intervals():"], [2.47, "\n    assert merge_intervals([[1,"], [2.5171, " 4], [4, 5"], [2.5641, "]]) == [[1, 5]]"], [2.6112, "\n\ndef test_unsorted_input():\n"], [2.6581, "    assert merge_intervals([[8"], [2.705, ", 10], [1,"], [2.7518, " 3], [2, 6"], [2.7993, "]]) == [[1, 6],"], [2.8465, " [8, 10]]\n"], [2.8943, "```\n\n**How it works"]], "tokens": 400}, {"prompt": "Explain how a CPU cache works to a new programmer, in three short paragraphs.", "chunks": [[0.1316, "Think"], [0.1715, " of your CPU as"], [0.258, " a super-fast chef and"], [0.3546, " your main memory ("], [0.4048, "RAM) as a distant warehouse. The"], [0.4555, " CPU cache"], [0.5066, " is essentially a small, high"], [0.5577, "-speed counter right next to the chef"], [0.6091, " where they keep the ingredients"], [0.6608, " they are currently using. Because the counter"], [0.7126, " is right there"], [0.7645, ", the chef can grab an"], [0.8171, " ingredient instantly"], [0.8692, ", whereas going to the warehouse takes"], [0.9222, " a lot"], [0.9752, " of time. This speed"], [1.0281, " difference is crucial because the CPU processes"], [1.0808, " data much faster than it can retrieve"], [1.133, " it from RAM.\n\nTo"], [1.1847, " make this work"], [1.2358, ", the system"], [1.2873, " uses a strategy called \"local"], [1.3385, "ity of reference.\""], [1.3895, " It assumes that if the"], [1.4411, " CPU accesses a"], [1.492, " specific piece of data,"], [1.5432, " it is likely to access nearby"], [1.5944, " data soon. So"], [1.6456, ", when the CPU requests"], [1.6964, " one item"], [1.7481, ", the system loads a whole block"], [1.7996, " of related data into the cache"], [1.8477, " at once. This way"], [1.8956, ", if the CPU needs the"], [1.9441, " next item in the sequence"], [1.9927, ", it\u2019s already sitting"], [2.0416, " on the fast"], [2.0902, " counter, ready to"], [2.1385, " be used without waiting for the"], [2.1863, " slow warehouse trip"], [2.2341, ".\n\nHowever, this counter"], [2.2808, " has limited space,"], [2.3284, " so it can\u2019t hold everything"], [2.3755, ". When it gets"], [2.4232, " full, the system has to decide what"], [2.4702, " to throw away to"], [2.5174, " make room for new data,"], [2.5642, " a process known as cache"], [2.6113, " eviction. If the CPU needs"], [2.6581, " data that was just thrown out"], [2.7051, ", it has to go back"], [2.752, " to the slow RAM"], [2.7995, " to fetch it again,"], [2.8467, " causing a \"cache miss.\" Program"], [2.895, "mers write code"], [2.9364, " with this in"], [2.9774, " mind, struct"], [3.0185, "uring data so that frequently"], [3.0597, " used items stay"], [3.101, " close together, ensuring"], [3.1422, " the cache stays full of"], [3.1839, " useful information and the CPU runs"], [3.2243, " as fast as possible."]], "tokens": 306}, {"prompt": "Write a SQL query that returns the top 3 customers by total order value per country, with a short explanation.", "chunks": [[0.2133, "```"], [0.2582, "sql\nWITH customer"], [0.3546, "_totals AS (\n   "], [0.4048, " SELECT\n        c.country"], [0.4556, ",\n        c.customer_id,\n"], [0.5067, "        c.customer_name,\n        SUM"], [0.5578, "(o.order_value) AS total_order_value"], [0.6092, "\n    FROM customers c\n    JOIN"], [0.661, " orders o ON c.customer_id = o"], [0.7127, ".customer_id\n    GROUP BY c.country"], [0.7646, ", c.customer_id, c.customer_name"], [0.8172, "\n),\nranked AS (\n"], [0.8693, "    SELECT\n        country,\n       "], [0.9223, " customer_id,\n        customer_name,"], [0.9752, "\n        total_order_value,\n       "], [1.0283, " RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY"], [1.0808, " country ORDER BY total_order_value DESC)"], [1.1331, " AS rnk\n    FROM"], [1.1847, " customer_totals\n)\nSELECT\n   "], [1.2359, " country,\n    customer_id,\n"], [1.2874, "    customer_name,\n    total_order"], [1.3386, "_value\nFROM ranked\nWHERE rnk"], [1.3899, " <= 3\nORDER BY country,"], [1.4413, " rnk;\n```"], [1.4923, "\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n1. **"], [1.5435, "`customer_totals` CTE**:"], [1.5947, " Joins `"], [1.6459, "customers` and `orders`, then groups"], [1.6966, " by country and customer to compute"], [1.7484, " each customer's total order"], [1.7998, " value within their country.\n\n"], [1.8482, "2. **`ranked` C"], [1.8961, "TE**: Uses the `"], [1.9445, "RANK()` window function partition"], [1.9932, "ed by `country` and ordered by"], [2.042, " `total_order_value` in descending order"], [2.0906, ". `RANK()` ("], [2.1389, "rather than `ROW_NUMBER()`) is"], [2.1866, " used so that ties in"], [2.2344, " total order value are all"], [2.2811, " included,"], [2.3287, " ensuring no customer is arbitrarily"], [2.3758, " excluded if multiple customers share the same"], [2.4235, " top value.\n\n3."], [2.4706, " **Final `SELECT`**: Filters"], [2.5177, " to only the top "], [2.5646, "3 ranks per country and"], [2.6115, " orders the results by country"], [2.6585, " and rank for readability"], [2.7055, ".\n\n> **Note:**"], [2.7523, " Adjust table and"], [2.7998, " column names (`customers`, `orders"], [2.8471, "`, `customer_id`, `order"], [2.8953, "_value`, `country`, `"], [2.9367, "customer_name`) to match your actual schema"], [2.9777, ". If you"], [3.019, " want exactly"], [3.0601, " 3 rows per country"], [3.1014, " even with ties,"], [3.1426, " replace `RANK()`"], [3.1843, " with `ROW_NUMBER()`."]], "tokens": 381}, {"prompt": "A train leaves at 9:40 and travels 210 km at 84 km/h. When does it arrive? Show the steps briefly.", "chunks": [[0.306, "Here"], [0.3547, " are the steps"], [0.4049, " to determine the arrival time:"], [0.4557, "\n\n**1. Calculate the"], [0.5068, " travel time**\n$$"], [0.5578, " \\text{Time} = \\frac"], [0.6093, "{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{"], [0.6609, "Speed}} $$\n$$ \\text{"], [0.7128, "Time} = \\frac{21"], [0.7647, "0 \\text{ km}}{8"], [0.8173, "4 \\text{ km/h}} ="], [0.8694, " 2.5 \\text{ hours"], [0.9223, "} $$\n\n**2. Convert decimal"], [0.9753, " hours to minutes**\n$$ "], [1.0283, "0.5 \\text{ hours}"], [1.0811, " \